From e152c869a0431d14bb5533f4b18838f18dae57f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:45:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mcp): hole patterns from numbers for Drill, Bore and
 Thread

Add camcraft_geometry::hole_pattern: a point list, a line, a grid and a
full or partial bolt-hole circle give hole centres by plain
trigonometry. Bad numbers are refused by the field name.

Add the MCP tool add_hole_pattern. It makes a Drill, Bore or Thread
operation on the stock with the pattern's holes, with no 3D model. The
holes start at the stock top unless "top" is given. Model-referenced
heights measure from the stock, so a stock-only setup generates. An
optional spot drill on the same holes comes first. The two operations
are one undo step. A refusal changes nothing.

Fixes #3195

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
